Handoff complete: yeh full design hai, execution nahi. Koi experiment run nahi hua aur koi outcome claim nahi kiya gaya.", "evidence": "Repository observations (executed): /workspace contains only task.json (design-only track confirmed by its documents.track.md note); no TorchOpt source/docs present. Python 3.14.4 system, pip 25.1.1; `import torch` and `import torchopt` both fail; pip download fails due to disabled network; no pip cache or torch wheels found. These findings ground the design's feasibility section (install prerequisite) and the source-unverified limitation. Design incorporates researcher's two locked decisions: B1 (unrolled create_graph=True) as primary baseline with B2 context-only, and a non-negotiable correctness precondition (B1 vs T gradient equality within rtol=1e-5/atol=1e-6 in float32, rtol=1e-7/atol=1e-9 in float64) gating timing. Flagged items from plan stage (install prerequisite, CPU memory-profiling limits, possible "no stability difference" outcome) are carried into §8 Explicit Limitations as requested. No experiment was run; no outcomes claimed.", "assumptions": [], "uncertainties": ["TorchOpt's internal implementation of the explicit-gradient API could not be inspected (source absent from /workspace); the reuse/allocation claims are documented hypotheses to be tested, not verified facts.", "Execution requires a provisioned or network-enabled environment with Python 3.10-3.12; torch wheel availability for the current Python 3.14 is unknown.", "The explicit API and B1 autograd unroll may produce bit-identical outputs in benign conditions, so any stability difference may only appear under W4 stress conditions, or not at all.", "CPU-only memory profiling (tracemalloc + torch profiler) is a proxy with limited precision; memory-allocation conclusions will be scoped accordingly.", "If the correctness precondition fails (A2 false), the treatment arm's definition must be revisited before any timing conclusions are valid."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-6168bafb1a7c44e1ac3281e87431d361", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-6168bafb1a7c44e1ac3281e87431d361", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"answer": "# Final Experiment Design \u2014 TorchOpt Explicit Gradient API: Speed & Numerical Stability\n\n**Question:** Kya TorchOpt ka explicit gradient differentiation API (intermediate data reuse + minimized memory allocation) standard autograd implementations se faster hai aur numerically zyada stable?\n\n**Status:** Design-only. Koi experiment run nahi hua. TorchOpt source `/workspace` mein absent tha, is liye API behavior documented claims se derived hai aur experiment mein hypothesis ki tarah test hoga.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Locked Decisions (researcher-approved)\n\n1. **Primary comparison = T vs B1.** \"Standard autograd\" ka primary interpretation **unrolled `torch.autograd.grad(..., create_graph=True)` unroll (B1)** hai. B2 (single-step `backward()`) sirf context/reference arm hai \u2014 iska result primary verdict mein nahi jayega.\n2. **Correctness precondition non-negotiable:** B1 vs T gradients har workload pe timing se **pehle** tolerance ke andar equal hone chahiye. Jo (arm, workload) fail kare, wo timing analysis mein include hi nahi hoga (aur uska failure khud report hoga \u2014 silent exclusion nahi).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Arms\n\n| Arm | Implementation | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| **T** | TorchOpt explicit path: `torchopt.diff(..., mode='explicit')` / `torchopt.diff.explicit(...)`, gradients inner loop se explicitly extract karke outer loop mein pass; TorchOpt optimizers (e.g., `torchopt.adam`) inner update ke liye | Treatment |\n| **B1** | Unrolled inner loop with `torch.autograd.grad(..., create_graph=True)`; updates hand-written, same math as T | **Primary baseline** |\n| **B2** | Standard per-step `loss.backward()` + `optimizer.step()` + `zero_grad()` (flat, non-unrolled loop) | Context only |\n| **B3** | Hand-rolled `torch.func.grad` + manual functional update (functorch, no TorchOpt) | Ablation \u2014 isolates TorchOpt wrapper benefit vs functorch-inherited benefit |\n| **B4 (optional)** | `torchopt.diff(..., mode='implicit')` | Secondary context; agar runtime budget tight ho to drop-able |\n\n**Fairness invariant:** T, B1, B3 mathematically same update rule execute karein (same inner optimizer, same step sizes, same unroll length). Yeh precondition check (\u00a74) se enforce hota hai.\n\n## 2. Workloads\n\n| ID | Task | Kyun | Speed target | Stability target |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **W1** | MAML-style inner-loop adaptation: MLP on synthetic sinusoid regression, K=5 inner steps, batched tasks | TorchOpt explicit API ka canonical use case (meta-learning unroll) | Yes | Yes \u2014 outer gradient vs float64 ref |\n| **W2** | Unrolled hyperparameter optimization: L2-regularized logistic regression, learning-rate as differentiable hyperparameter, T=10 unroll steps | Analytic/near-analytic reference solution available; ill-conditioning controllable (\u03bb sweep) | Yes | Yes \u2014 primary reference-anchored check |\n| **W3** | Deep-chain stress: 20-layer MLP, unroll K=10\u201320, hidden 256 | Long unroll + many intermediates: memory allocation aur numerical drift dono amplify | Yes | Yes \u2014 drift growth vs K |\n| **W4** | Stability-only sweep: W2 variants with (a) ill-conditioned design matrix (condition number 10\u00b3\u201310\u2076), (b) K \u2208 {1,2,4,8,16,32}, (c) float32 | Sensitivity analysis; speed timings secondary | No | Yes |\n\nScale guardrail: har workload \u2264 ~1M parameters, CPU-feasible seconds-per-iteration.\n\n## 3. Controls\n\n- **Seeds & pairing:** Har repeat ka fixed seed set (`torch.manual_seed`, `numpy.random.seed`). Sab arms same seed, same init, same data, same schedule receive karte hain \u2192 paired observations.\n- **Correctness precondition (gate):** Har (arm, workload) pe, timing se pehle: T aur B1 ke outer gradients ko ek common seed pe compare karo (`torch.allclose(rtol=1e-5, atol=1e-6)`; float64 runs pe `rtol=1e-7`). Fail \u2192 exclude from timing + report.\n- **Warmup:** 3 untimed warmup iterations per arm per workload (JIT/allocator/graph-cache warm-up).\n- **Timing repeats:** \u22655 timed repeats per (arm, workload); har repeat mein fresh state (no cross-repeat graph reuse).\n- **Threading:** `torch.set_num_threads(8)` fixed throughout; environment variable thread-pool settings (`OMP_NUM_THREADS` etc.) pinned. 224-core machine pe jitter control ke liye zaroori.\n- **Timing methodology:** `time.perf_counter` around full outer iteration (inner loop + gradient computation + update); additionally `torch.utils.benchmark` se cross-check. Per-iteration time report karo, cumulative nahi.\n- **Memory:** `tracemalloc` peak (Python-level) + `torch.autograd.profiler.profile(profile_memory=True)` se torch tensor allocation peaks. Same measurement method sab arms pe.\n- **dtype:** Stability comparisons float32 mein (deployment-realistic); float64 reference alag compute hota hai; dtype sensitivity (\u00a72 W4c) alag run.\n- **Identical-output sanity:** Iteration-0 ke baad sab arms ka loss/params bit-close hon \u2014 agar init-level differences hain to harness bug hai, experiment invalid.\n\n## 4. Numerical Tolerance Criteria (explicit)\n\n- **Cross-arm gradient agreement (precondition):** float32: `rtol=1e-5, atol=1e-6` on outer gradients; float64: `rtol=1e-7, atol=1e-9`.\n- **Reference agreement (stability):** float64 reference gradient ke against max relative error (component-wise, `|\u0394|/(|ref|+\u03b5)`); threshold per workload define hoga (initial value: 1e-3 float32 for K\u226410; W4 mein drift-curve ke roop mein report, single pass/fail nahi).\n- **NaN/Inf:** koi bhi NaN/Inf arm ki stability failure; count reported.\n- **Drift growth:** log(max-rel-error) vs K ka linear-regression slope \u2014 growth rate metric, arms ke beech compare.\n\n## 5. Analysis Plan\n\n- **Primary speed metric:** median wall-clock time per outer iteration (over \u22655 repeats), bootstrap 95% CI (10k resamples). Report speed ratio B1/T per workload with CI.\n- **\"Faster\" verdict:** T ka median time B1 se significantly kam ho **aur** yeh advantage \u22653 workloads mein consistent ho (CI non-overlapping). Agar mixed results \u2192 per-workload report, blanket claim nahi.\n- **Primary memory metric:** peak allocated memory per outer iteration (torch profiler), same CI treatment. tracemalloc secondary/consistency check.\n- **Primary stability metric:** (a) NaN/Inf incidence, (b) max-rel-error vs float64 ref, (c) drift slope vs K. \n- **\"More stable\" verdict:** T strictly better tabhi jab B1 kisi workload pe NaN/Inf ya threshold-exceeding drift dikhaye aur T na dikaye. Agar dono thresholds ke andar hain \u2192 **\"numerically equivalent\"** report karo (ye genuinely possible outcome hai, \u00a78 dekho).\n- **Ablation read:** T vs B3 ka speed/memory delta batata hai ki benefit TorchOpt-specific hai (wrapper, reuse logic) ya functorch-inherited (functional transforms). B1 vs B3 bhi interesting hai (autograd-unroll vs functional-unroll).\n- **Statistical note:** Paired-by-seed differences report karo (within-repeat deltas), sirf independent-sample comparison nahi \u2014 CPU noise variance kam karta hai.\n\n## 6. Feasibility (CPU-only)\n\n- Workloads small (\u22641M params, synthetic) \u2014 CPU pe per-iteration seconds, total run hours-scale. 224 cores available; hum 8 threads pin karenge (oversubscription se bachne ke liye).\n- No GPU required \u2014 in fact GPU exclude karna claims ko CPU-scoped rakhta hai (memory-allocation behavior device-specific hota hai; results ko \"CPU-only\" ke roop mein scope karna honest hai).\n- **Prerequisite (blocker for execution, not for design):** `torch` + `torchopt` install chahiye. Current env: Python 3.14.4, no network, no wheels. Actual run ke liye network-enabled ya pre-provisioned env with Python 3.10\u20133.12 chahiye. Versions pinned honge (torch version + torchopt version dono, kyunki torch.func/functorch API versions ke beech badalta hai).\n\n## 7. Deliverables (jab run ho)\n\n1. Harness script (arms + workloads + controls + precondition gate).\n2. Raw timings/memory CSV (arm, workload, seed, repeat, iteration, metrics).\n3. Results table: speed ratio, memory ratio, stability metrics per workload.\n4. Precondition-check report (koi arm fail hua?).\n5. One-page verdict: faster? more stable? numerically equivalent? \u2014 scoped to CPU-only, tested workloads, pinned versions.\n\n## 8. Explicit Limitations & Uncertainties\n\n1. **Source unverified:** TorchOpt ka implementation inspect nahi ho sakta tha; \"intermediate reuse + minimized allocation\" documented claim par based hypothesis hai. Agar run mein pata chalta hai ki explicit API internally wahi autograd graph banata hai, to speed/memory differences zero ya negative ho sakte hain \u2014 yeh valid outcome hai.\n2. **Install prerequisite:** Network-disabled env mein torch/torchopt install nahi ho sakte; Python 3.14 pe torch wheel availability bhi uncertain. Execution ko provisioned env chahiye.\n3. **Possible \"no stability difference\" outcome:** Agar T aur B1 same ops same order mein chalate hain, outputs bit-identical ho sakte hain \u2014 stability difference sirf W4-style stress (long unroll, ill-conditioning, float32) mein materialize hoga, ho sakta hai na ho.\n4. **Memory profiling precision on CPU:** torch ka allocation accounting CPU pe GPU jitna precise nahi; tracemalloc Python-level only hai. Memory-allocation claims partially testable \u2014 conclusions ko \"as measured by these proxies\" scope karenge.\n5. **Scope limits:** CPU-only results GPU claims par generalize nahi honge; synthetic workloads real meta-learning scale ka proxy hain, production-scale MAML nahi.\n6. **Version sensitivity:** torch.func API evolution ke saath TorchOpt behavior change ho sakta hai; findings pinned versions tak valid.\n\n## 9. Key Assumptions (stated separately, unverified)\n\n- **A1:** TorchOpt documented claim (reuse + less allocation) explicit mode pe sach hai.\n- **A2:** `torchopt.diff.explicit` ka computed math unrolled `create_graph=True` ke barabar hai (precondition ise verify karega; agar galat sabit ho to design ka T-arm definition revisit hoga \u2014 ye failure mode report-worthy hai, hide nahi).\n- **A3:** Network-enabled install actual run ke liye available hoga.\n- **A4:** \"Standard autograd implementation\" = B1 (locked by researcher).\n\n---\n\nHandoff complete: yeh full design hai, execution nahi. Koi experiment run nahi hua aur koi outcome claim nahi kiya gaya.", "evidence": "Repository observations (executed): /workspace contains only task.json (design-only track confirmed by its documents.track.md note); no TorchOpt source/docs present. Python 3.14.4 system, pip 25.1.1; `import torch` and `import torchopt` both fail; pip download fails due to disabled network; no pip cache or torch wheels found. These findings ground the design's feasibility section (install prerequisite) and the source-unverified limitation. Design incorporates researcher's two locked decisions: B1 (unrolled create_graph=True) as primary baseline with B2 context-only, and a non-negotiable correctness precondition (B1 vs T gradient equality within rtol=1e-5/atol=1e-6 in float32, rtol=1e-7/atol=1e-9 in float64) gating timing. Flagged items from plan stage (install prerequisite, CPU memory-profiling limits, possible \"no stability difference\" outcome) are carried into \u00a78 Explicit Limitations as requested. No experiment was run; no outcomes claimed.", "stage": "result", "summary": "Handed off complete approved experiment design document", "uncertainties": ["TorchOpt's internal implementation of the explicit-gradient API could not be inspected (source absent from /workspace); the reuse/allocation claims are documented hypotheses to be tested, not verified facts.", "Execution requires a provisioned or network-enabled environment with Python 3.10-3.12; torch wheel availability for the current Python 3.14 is unknown.", "The explicit API and B1 autograd unroll may produce bit-identical outputs in benign conditions, so any stability difference may only appear under W4 stress conditions, or not at all.", "CPU-only memory profiling (tracemalloc + torch profiler) is a proxy with limited precision; memory-allocation conclusions will be scoped accordingly.", "If the correctness precondition fails (A2 false), the treatment arm's definition must be revisited before any timing conclusions are valid."]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-6cdac045b5774bae9db68400f11fcbc6", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Handed off complete approved experiment design document", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
